<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.14.5: Identifying Key Features of Graphed Functions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01985</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.14.5: Identifying Key Features of Graphed Functions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>67a55d7d-f99b-4a64-958c-5f3dec8725b3</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<title>Launch</title>
<para>Provide continued access to graphing technology, in case students choose to use it.</para>
<title>Student Activity</title>
<para>The equation \(y=(-16t−2)(t−1)\) represents the height in feet of a beach ball thrown by a child as a function of time, \(t\), in seconds.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Since the equation is in factored form, we can tell that the graph intersects the horizontal axis at two points. Use this information to find the zeros of the function. Explain or show your reasoning.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item> Find one of the zeros of the functions using \((-16t−2)\). </item>
  </list>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> -0.125 or \(-\frac{1}{8}\). From the factored form, we can tell that the graph intersects the horizontal axis at \(t=-0.125\) or \(-\frac{1}{8}\). The zero of the function is the same value.</para>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item> Find one of the zeros of the functions using \((t−1)\). </item>
  </list>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 1. From the factored form, we can tell that the graph intersects the horizontal axis at \(t=1\). The zero of the function is the same value.</para>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>What do the zeros tell us in this situation?</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> The zeros mean the time in seconds when the ball is on the ground.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>Are both zeros meaningful?</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>No. Only one of them is meaningful. The negative zero doesn't mean anything here.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>From what height, in feet, is the beach ball thrown? Explain or show your reasoning.</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 2. The height when \(t=0\) is \((-16(0)−2)(0−1)=(-2)(-1)=2\). If you graph the function, the graph shows a \(y\)-intercepts of \((0,2)\).</para>
<title>Response to Student Thinking</title>
<title>Press Pause</title>
<para>If students struggle to interpret functions in context, plan to spend extra time on this topic before the assessment by reviewing activities and practice problems.</para></section>
</content>
</document>
